Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||01-23-2001||03:02 PM||||Another point to add.<BR>The brake system for the '88 model year was up graded by the factory. The draw back no is that the componets for them are hard to find and expensive.<BR>Hope this helps your frustrations!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black88GT||01-23-2001||05:07 PM||||Use the search function and find a post about rear rotors you can get for 15 bucks at AutoZone (so much for being hard to find and expensive).  They are stock, but the reason people do the Grand Am brake swap is to have vented rotors (I'm pretty sure) which the 88's already have.  In addition, they lose their e-brake.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||01-23-2001||06:13 PM||||The brakes are already awesome so why would you want to upgrade them?||||reg||1
